<title>SINGAPORE: Thai refiner Rayong sells Apr gasoline to Shell.</title>
<headline>Thai refiner Rayong sells Apr gasoline to Shell.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai refiner Rayong Refinery Co Ltd has sold in a tender 230,000 barrels of 95-octane unleaded gasoline to Shell Singapore at around $1.00 per barrel below Singapore 95-octane spot quotes, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The cargo for lifting on April 17 was sold on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>Rayong Refinery is 60-percent owned by Shell with state-owned Petroleum Authority of Thailand (PTT) taking the remaining 40 percent.</p>
<p>The tender closed April 8 and was valid for the same day.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
